- [P2] Serialize tests that mutate shared region state — /home/yuu/Documents/Codex/2026-10-04/mc/outputs/mc-spine/native/src/tick_tests.rs:51-54
  With the default parallel Rust test runner, this test races with `game_tick_progresses_warm_furnace_and_keeps_cold_furnace_unchanged`: both replace and mutate the same global `forceloaded`, `hot`, and `warm` sets. Individual mutex acquisitions do not isolate the complete fixtures. For example, this test can clear the furnace test's forced chunk before `game_tick`, leaving its furnace cold, or the furnace test can overwrite region membership between `refresh_hot` and an observation. This introduces nondeterministic failures in ordinary `cargo test` runs. Hold a shared test-level lock across setup, execution, and restoration in both tests.
